Source: spell.inc
     1 				; Spell checker (Search > Spell check). Dictionary format and hash: docs/DICTIONARY.md.
     2 				; The dictionary (CDIC file) is read once: on a 130XE the 16 KB bit table goes into extended bank 1 (window
     3 				; $4000-$7FFF, switched in only inside bk_get / bk_put at $9300); on a stock 64K machine it is placed
     4 				; just below $9000, in the unused top of the document area, and released when the check ends.
     5 				; Words come from the document, letters and inner apostrophes, with style and paragraph codes skipped.
     6 				; Words with digits or non-ASCII characters, 1-letter words and words over 24 letters are not checked.
     7 				; The unknown word is shown inverse (style code 4 inserted around it, removed again before moving on).
     8
     9
